 only demonstrated prebiotic synthesis: surface aqueous-phase condensation of erythrose (from the formose reaction) with formamidine (from HCN/NH3), ring closure to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde, and Strecker-type cyanation/hydrolysis to histidine\u2014a contested, low-yield (3.5%) pathway shown experimentally by Shen, Yang, Miller & Or\u00f3 (1987, 1990). This is complemented by literature-derived and speculative branches from imidazole derivatives and semi-enzymatic biotic scenarios. Ten distinct pathways are explicitly represented: (1) canonical sugar+amidine route; (2\u20133) via imidazole-4-glycol/ethanol side products; (4) from prebiotic HCN-polymer hydrolysates (trace, unconfirmed); (5) speculative sequential Strecker from imidazole-4-acetaldehyde; (6) semi-enzymatic HisF/IGP-like assembly; (7\u20138) conversion of imidazole-4-carboxylic/pyruvic acid intermediates (hypothetical hydrothermal/meteoritic); (9) Debus condensation (wrong regioisomer, side-branch); (10) C2\u2013C2 coupling (cyanosulfidic, speculative). The bottleneck is standing up the C4 sugar+amidine condensation; all mineral and environmental assignments are justified per the evidence, with contested and hypothetical links flagged. No cross-environment transfer is proposed without plausible chemical rationale.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_001\",\n      \"formula\": \"H2CO\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"methanal\",\n      \"common_name\": \"formaldehyde\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CH2O/c1-2/h1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_002\",\n      \"formula\": \"NH3\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"azane\",\n      \"common_name\": \"ammonia\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/H3N/h1H3\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_003\",\n      \"formula\": \"HCN\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"common_name\": null,\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CHN/c1-2/h1H\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_004\",\n      \"formula\": \"C4H8O4\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2,3,4-trihydroxybutanal\",\n      \"common_name\": \"erythrose\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C4H8O4/c5-1-2(6)3(7)4-8/h2-4,6-8H,1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_005\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH4N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"formamidine\",\n      \"common_name\": null,\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CH4N2/c2-1-3/h1H,(H4,2,3)\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_006\",\n      \"formula\": \"C5H7N3O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-amino-1H-imidazole-4-ethanal\",\n      \"common_name\": \"imidazole-4-acetaldehyde\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C5H7N3O/c6-5-7-3(1-4-9)2-8-5/h1-2,4H,6H2,(H,7,8)\",\n      \"role\": \"hub_intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_007\",\n      \"formula\": \"C5H7N3O2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-amino-1H-imidazole-4-hydroxyacetaldehyde\",\n      \"common_name\": \"imidazole-4-glycol\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C5H7N3O2/c6-5-7-3(1-4(9)10)2-8-5/h1-2,4,9-10H,6H2,(H,7,8)\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_008\",\n      \"formula\": \"C5H9N3O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-amino-1H-imidazole-4-ethanol\",\n      \"common_name\": \"imidazole-4-ethanol\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C5H9N3O/c6-5-7-3(1-4-9)2-8-5/h1-2,4,9H,6H2,(H,7,8)\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_009\",\n      \"formula\": \"C6H9N3O2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-amino-3-(1H-imidazol-4-yl)propanoic acid\",\n      \"common_name\": \"histidine\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C6H9N3O2/c7-5-2-9-4(