tion from imidazole-4-acetaldehyde reservoir (side pathway)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_016, mol_015, mol_002 -> mol_009 (Semi-enzymatic (biotic-like) assembly of histidine via IGP) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_010: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_013 (Debus-type condensation: imidazole ring formation from glyoxal, aldehyde, and ammonia (side product)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_011: mol_010, mol_002 -> mol_006 (Decarboxylation/amination of imidazole-4-carboxylic acid to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde (hypothetical)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_012: mol_011, mol_002 -> mol_009 (Reductive amination of imidazole-4-pyruvic acid (hypothetical)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_013: mol_001, mol_003, mol_002, mol_005 -> mol_006 (C2\u2013C2 coupling of HCN/amidine to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde (cyanosulfidic speculative)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_012 -> mol_006 (Conversion of imidazole-4-ethylamine to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde (hypothetical oxidative deamination)) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Canonical surface sugar-amidine condensation (4 steps)\n  - P2: Imidazole-4-glycol oxidation branch (5 steps)\n  - P3: Imidazole-4-ethanol oxidation branch (5 steps)\n  - P4: HCN polymer hydrolysate (trace histidine/imidazole) (1 steps)\n  - P5: Alternate Strecker from imidazole-4-acetaldehyde reservoirs (1 steps)\n  - P6: Semi-enzymatic biotic histidine synthesis (1 steps)\n  - P7: Meteorite/bennu-derived imidazole-4-carboxylic acid conversion (speculative hydrothermal) (2 steps)\n  - P8: Imidazole-4-pyruvate hydrothermal branch (hypothetical) (1 steps)\n  - P9: Debus condensation: direct imidazole ring from H2CO and NH3 (side regioisomer route) (1 steps)\n  - P10: C2\u2013C2 coupling (cyanosulfidic speculative) (2 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\n