nks \u2014 imidazole-4-glycol and imidazole-4-ethanol \u2014 are represented, as are hypothetical (unproven) routes from HCN polymer hydrolysis and a late-stage biotic, IGP-like pathway. All transformations are enforced to be atom- and charge-balanced, with explicit water/ammonia generation or consumption where necessary, following organic/physical chemical precedent. The hydrothermal and cyanosulfidic hypotheses are modelled only at the precursor or imidazole-carboxylate level, as literature shows no atom-economical, selective path to histidine from these starting points. Conversion of side-pathway intermediates is marked as speculative. The network critically weighs the severe limitations on tetrose/formamidine co-availability, the highly inefficient conversion overall, and the absence of evidence for alternative or more robust routes. Each reaction is fully specified and, if speculative, denoted as such.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "CH2O", "iupac_name": "methanal", "common_name": "formaldehyde", "inchi": "InChI=1S/CH2O/c1-2/h1H2", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_002", "formula": "NH3", "iupac_name": "azane", "common_name": "ammonia", "inchi": "InChI=1S/H3N/h1H3", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_003", "formula": "HCN", "iupac_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "common_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "inchi": "InChI=1S/CHN/c1-2/h1H", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_004", "formula": "C4H8O4", "iupac_name": "tetrahydroxybutanal", "common_name": "erythrose", "inchi": "InChI=1S/C4H8O4/c5-1-2(6)3(7)4(8)9/h2-4,6-8H,1H2", "role": "intermediate", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_005", "formula": "CH4N2", "iupac_name": "formamidine", "common_name": "formamidine", "inchi": "InChI=1S/CH4N2/c2-1-3/h1-2H,3H2", "role": "intermediate", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_006", "formula": "C5H7N3O", "iupac_name": "2,5-dihydro-1H-imidazole-4-acetaldehyde"